// An untyped `[]` read only as an element of another list literal. The
// frontend admits it, and the go reference REFUSES it by name: there is no
// declared List type anywhere the binding flows, and Go fixes a composite
// literal's element type at the literal (issue #2898).
//
// An element position is not a flow target: the outer `[row]` types its own
// element from its items, and an itemless `row` names no element type, so the
// inner literal has neither a target, nor pushed evidence, nor any read the
// only-sized fallback allows (its one read is the element position itself).
// The reference refuses instead of printing `[]any{}` and letting `go build`
// reject the module.
//
// Not a byte-agreement case, so it cannot live in the tier's CORPUS.
fn w() -> List[List[Int]] {
  var row = []
  return [row]
}
